> constraints for shadcn and Tailwind. Shared primitives live in `packages/ui`.

# Product Design System

Before changing UI in `apps/dashboard` or `packages/ui`, prefer existing shadcn
primitives and Tailwind tokens in `packages/ui` over one-off markup.

## Must

- Compose theme and base styles once at the app root (CSS variables / Tailwind
  theme from `packages/ui`, not a second competing theme system).
- Use shadcn primitives from `packages/ui` before bespoke controls. Add a wrapper
  only for reusable behavior or a named product semantic.
- Prefer Tailwind utility classes and shared CSS variables for layout, color,
  spacing, and typography. Keep static CSS for narrow layout needs.
- Preserve accessible focus, hover, pressed, disabled, validation, keyboard, and
  reduced-motion behavior from the underlying Radix / shadcn primitives.
- Use TanStack Table (headless) plus TanStack Virtual for the explore grid, and
  Recharts via shadcn charts for overview charts. Do not introduce a second
  grid or chart stack without confirmation.
- Communicate severity and status with text or icon, not color alone.
- Keep filtering, sorting, suggestions, pagination, and export in the browser
  Web Worker, not render code.

## Must Not

- Import a second UI framework (for example Material UI) alongside shadcn.
- Put product features, GraphQL operations, routing, domain logic, producer
  code, or app-only imports in `packages/ui`.
- Bypass `packages/ui` with relative copies of shadcn components inside
  `apps/dashboard` when the shared package already exports them.
- Invent a dark theme as a default mode; polarity-flipped ink is a surface
  treatment only when the product explicitly defines it.
- Create pass-through styled wrappers that add no behavior.
- Replace form-field semantics with a non-semantic styled container.

